Visual Sketches Bootcamp is dual-licensed by file scope.

Curriculum content — CC BY 4.0
================================

Unless a file or nearby attribution record says otherwise, original curriculum
prose and course media are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0), included at:

    LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

This scope includes Markdown and other instructional text, authoring metadata,
original diagrams, transcripts, images, and audiovisual course media. When
attributing this material, identify “Visual Sketches Bootcamp contributors,”
link to this repository when practical, link or refer to CC BY 4.0, and indicate
whether changes were made.

Software — MIT
==============

Unless a file says otherwise, source code and supporting software are licensed
under the MIT License, included at:

    LICENSES/MIT.txt

This scope includes C/C++ source and headers, tests, shell and PowerShell
scripts, CI workflow definitions, Hugo layouts, site styles/configuration, and
build/project metadata.

Original fixture data — CC0 1.0
==============================

Hand-authored numerical and synthetic test data whose nearby fixture README
identifies CC0-1.0 is dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal,
included at:

    LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt

The nearby fixture README controls when it states this more specific scope.
Fixture parser/test source code remains MIT-licensed.

Exclusions and third-party material
===================================

These licenses apply only to material for which the repository contributors
hold the necessary rights. They do not relicense:

- openFrameworks, addons, tools, libraries, or other dependencies;
- linked or quoted upstream documentation, tutorials, and source material;
- third-party or public-domain assets identified by an `assets.yaml`,
  `ATTRIBUTION.md`, source header, notice, or other nearby record; or
- learner submissions and externally contributed media that state separate
  terms.

Those works remain under their respective terms. Preserve all copyright,
license, attribution, modification, source, and notice requirements. See
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` for bundled code patterns with retained notices. If a
file’s nearby notice conflicts with this top-level scope, the specific notice
controls for that file.
